WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:13.160
Hi, welcome back to the Wheel of Life at-home retreat.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:20.360
We have reached session 13.

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:25.760
That's called "Life in the womb."

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:32.760
What's happened is, we finished the first two

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:35.080
of the twelve links of The Wheel of Life.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:44.840
As you remember, link number one was misunderstanding things.

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:51.920
If misunderstanding could talk,

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:58.080
it would walk in the kitchen and when the husband yells,

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:05.920
it would say, "I didn't do anything! Why you yelling at me?"

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:10.120
That's perfect link number one,

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:15.040
and it causes all the trouble in our life.

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:22.880
Then that, "I didn't do anything, but he yelled at me."

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:26.520
That's perfect link number one

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:28.960
misunderstanding talking.

00:01:31.640 --> 00:01:36.320
And that triggers the twelve links--tsk tsk tsk ...

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:43.760
I like his translation of "tsk tsk tsk."

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:49.000
So it triggers each one

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:51.600
and so "I didn't do anything,"

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:55.560
then that misunderstanding

00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:58.760
triggers the second link.

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:03.760
The second link says, "I'm not stupid, you're stupid!"

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:08.920
Because we have misunderstanding

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:11.760
we make karma,

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:15.000
we plant new seeds.

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:17.080
Now link number three,

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:20.760
as you see the picture ...

00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:21.960
by the way,

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:23.880
we started with a child in the womb,

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:32.120
which is the general theme of this whole session 13.

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:37.480
But, now we're going to go to link number three.

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:41.920
It's called "consciousness"

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:44.560
or you can say "awareness."

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:49.040
The traditional painting is a monkey.

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:55.520
Now listen, many years ago

00:02:57.280 --> 00:03:02.120
I was going to teach the Wheel of Life in Austin, Texas--it's a small city in Texas.

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:14.640
I was very excited and I thought ten people were coming.

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:18.720
And I said,

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:23.120
I'm gonna order a painting of the Wheel of Life for each person who comes.

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:32.000
Then I found a painter in Nepal.

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:36.520
He can paint for like a hundred dollars for each painting.

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:41.760
Then it will cost me a thousand dollars.

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:45.680
And I thought that's ok.

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:51.040
Then the organizer in Texas, (with accent) they talk like that in Texas,

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:54.880
She called me,

00:03:56.080 --> 00:03:57.120
"Oh Geshe-la,

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:00.080
yeah a hundred people coming!"

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:04.440
Then I am like, "Oh my god--that's ten thousand dollars!"

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:08.200
I called the painter in Nepal,

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:13.640
"Can we get a little bit cheaper paintings?"

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:18.520
He said, "How much?"

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:21.400
I said, "Well my budget is a thousand dollars and

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:23.840
I need to make a hundred paintings."

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:33.280
So to give each participant one painting,

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:39.720
they said, "Ha ha! For ten dollars, I won't even pick up my paintbrush."

00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:46.560
Then my friend heard about the problem.

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:50.680
"Geshe Michael, I have solution."

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:52.560
What?

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:57.480
"I know a school for children in Nepal where they teach painting."

00:05:03.520 --> 00:05:06.240
And I said, "Oh great--we can get the kids to paint."

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:11.080
Then this is the painting I got from the kids.

00:05:13.960 --> 00:05:18.000
And that's why each link is painted so badly.

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:25.720
But anyway you can tell, link number three is a monkey, right?

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:35.920
This represents your mind entering your mother's womb.

00:05:40.680 --> 00:05:42.680
Now let's go to the text.

00:05:45.640 --> 00:05:49.040
sumpa namshe la gyu du dang dre du kyi namshe nyi
(GSUM PA RNAM SHES LA RGYU DUS DANG 'BRAS DUS KYI RNAM SHES GNYIS)--

00:05:49.880 --> 00:05:51.880
now we reach link number three,

00:05:54.040 --> 00:05:56.040
which is consciousness.

00:05:57.000 --> 00:06:00.560
You can divide all consciousness into two kinds:

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:08.000
one is consciousness at the time of the cause,

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:16.040
and the second is consciousness at the time of the result.

00:06:18.360 --> 00:06:19.640
What does that mean?

00:06:21.040 --> 00:06:22.480
The text says: dangpo ni (DANG PO NI)--

00:06:22.880 --> 00:06:25.520
what is consciousness at the time of the cause?

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:32.760
du je kyi le kyi bakchak shak ma thakpay namshe dang
('DU BYED KYI LAS KYI BAG CHAGS BZHAG MA THAG PA'I RNAM SHES DANG)

00:06:33.680 --> 00:06:34.880
In link number two,

00:06:36.960 --> 00:06:39.880
the woman yelled back at her husband,

00:06:41.840 --> 00:06:44.120
"I'm not stupid--you're stupid!"

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:47.880
Those words came out of her mouth,

00:06:50.200 --> 00:06:52.000
touched the husband's ear,

00:06:53.560 --> 00:06:55.560
Then the husband (frowns).

00:06:56.520 --> 00:06:58.160
But those words also

00:06:59.080 --> 00:07:01.080
circle around to her own ear,

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:08.000
and they go into her mind

00:07:09.600 --> 00:07:11.200
and they make an imprint on the mind.

00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:16.120
That's what this book now says.

00:07:16.280 --> 00:07:18.760
du je kyi le kyi bakchak
('DU BYED KYI LAS KYI BAG CHAGS)

00:07:22.520 --> 00:07:25.280
bakchak (BAG CHAGS) is another word for "karmic seed,"

00:07:28.200 --> 00:07:30.880
And it's that imprint on the mind.

00:07:33.480 --> 00:07:34.840
It goes like this:

00:07:35.800 --> 00:07:37.760
misunderstand the husband,

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:38.920
link number one,

00:07:39.200 --> 00:07:40.880
"I didn't do anything!"

00:07:41.200 --> 00:07:41.920
Link number two,

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:44.640
"I'm not stupid--you're stupid!"

00:07:45.120 --> 00:07:46.000
Link number three

00:07:46.360 --> 00:07:48.160
is one second later.

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:52.000
That sound reaches her own mind

00:07:55.040 --> 00:07:56.800
and it makes an impression there--

00:07:56.840 --> 00:07:58.240
bakchak.

00:08:00.560 --> 00:08:03.120
The mind at that moment is called

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:06.080
the consciousness of the time of the cause.

00:08:10.760 --> 00:08:11.760
nyipa ni (GNYIS PA NI)

00:08:12.040 --> 00:08:14.920
What's the consciousness at the time of the result?

00:08:17.440 --> 00:08:21.240
kye si du nying tsam jar ma takpay du kyi namshe de yin
(SKYE SRID DU NYING MTSAMS SBYAR MA THAG PA'I DUS KYI RNAM SHES DE YIN)--

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:23.040
well, that's the monkey

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:25.920
and it's your

00:08:26.040 --> 00:08:27.040
awareness

00:08:27.200 --> 00:08:29.200
entered your mother's womb.

00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:37.400
Your mind at the moment that you plant a new seed,

00:08:41.680 --> 00:08:44.680
that's called consciousness at the time of the cause.

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:49.840
And consciousness at the time of the result,

00:08:50.680 --> 00:08:51.400
is just after

00:08:51.520 --> 00:08:53.320
your mind goes into your mother's womb and

00:08:54.120 --> 00:08:56.400
you make the crossing to that new life.

00:09:02.920 --> 00:09:04.720
Then Pabongka Rinpoche

00:09:04.720 --> 00:09:06.280
wants to give us an example.

00:09:09.280 --> 00:09:11.960
per na marikpe kun ne lang te
(DPER NA MA RIG PAS KUN NAS BSLANG STE)--

00:09:11.960 --> 00:09:13.280
Let's say that

00:09:14.040 --> 00:09:16.120
your motivation, your misunderstanding,

00:09:16.120 --> 00:09:18.680
pushes you to do something.

00:09:22.800 --> 00:09:26.680
There is a very common misunderstanding nowadays.

00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:31.520
If you want to be healthy,

00:09:33.240 --> 00:09:34.920
you have to eat a lot of protein,

00:09:36.080 --> 00:09:38.080
and the best place to get the protein

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:42.200
is to kill an animal

00:09:42.840 --> 00:09:44.840
and then they eat their body.

00:09:46.080 --> 00:09:47.400
This is

00:09:47.760 --> 00:09:50.080
motivated by misunderstanding.

00:09:53.120 --> 00:09:55.320
I became vegetarian

00:09:55.840 --> 00:09:57.640
about 35 years ago.

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:05.560
All my friends from Princeton University,

00:10:08.240 --> 00:10:14.280
they told me, "Oh, Mike, you're going to get sick! You don't have enough protein--you are not eating meat."

00:10:21.040 --> 00:10:23.480
I will tell you something true:

00:10:26.080 --> 00:10:28.080
All those guys are dead.

00:10:28.840 --> 00:10:30.840
They all had a heart attack,

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:33.080
diabetes,

00:10:34.440 --> 00:10:36.000
obese,

00:10:36.800 --> 00:10:39.200
because they eat too much meat.

00:10:40.680 --> 00:10:44.000
That's a kind of misunderstanding,

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:47.280
"I have to meat to be healthy."

00:10:50.520 --> 00:10:53.320
Then you pay people to kill that animal.

00:10:56.080 --> 00:10:56.480
So he says,

00:10:56.600 --> 00:10:58.480
sok chu kyi le dujepay tse
(SROG GCOD KYI LAS 'DU BYED PA'I TSE)--

00:10:58.800 --> 00:11:00.600
when someone kills the animal for you,

00:11:06.160 --> 00:11:07.080
and suppose

00:11:07.400 --> 00:11:10.320
le lam dzok (LAS LAM RDZOGS)...

00:11:11.160 --> 00:11:14.760
This le lam (LAS LAM) is a very exciting word

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:19.040
for all of you people who went to programs by DCI.

00:11:25.880 --> 00:11:27.080
The word le (LAS)

00:11:28.080 --> 00:11:29.160
means "karma."

00:11:30.200 --> 00:11:31.280
The word le lam

00:11:32.480 --> 00:11:34.360
means a "path of karma."

00:11:35.800 --> 00:11:36.640
For fifty dollars:

00:11:38.200 --> 00:11:41.400
what is the difference between karma and the path of karma?

00:11:45.200 --> 00:11:47.400
le lam means the complete four steps.

00:11:49.080 --> 00:11:51.160
le--karma--is the one that is not complete.

00:11:52.000 --> 00:11:54.040
Unfortunately, you are correct.

00:12:08.600 --> 00:12:09.840
Yes.

00:12:11.880 --> 00:12:14.800
How do you say, le lam?

00:12:19.720 --> 00:12:20.680
okay, le lam.

00:12:21.280 --> 00:12:22.520
So, dzokpa (RDZOGS PA)--

00:12:22.720 --> 00:12:25.000
let's say you kill the animal,

00:12:27.040 --> 00:12:29.000
all four steps were complete.

00:12:30.320 --> 00:12:31.800
What's the four steps?

00:12:33.280 --> 00:12:35.280
"I want protein so I can be healthy."

00:12:36.080 --> 00:12:40.440
Number one: say what you want.

00:12:41.320 --> 00:12:46.080
Number two: Who is going to be your bad seed planting partner?

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:49.200
A pig.

00:12:50.560 --> 00:12:53.960
Number three: How to do the bad deed?

00:12:55.760 --> 00:13:00.320
Pay the store to pay the guy to kill the pig,

00:13:00.640 --> 00:13:03.120
then you collected three new bad karmas!

00:13:08.720 --> 00:13:10.160
What's step four?

00:13:10.880 --> 00:13:13.040
"Oh, I'm so glad I ate the pork today.

00:13:15.360 --> 00:13:17.160
Now I will have muscle."

00:13:18.040 --> 00:13:22.120
That's a le lam dzok--

00:13:23.640 --> 00:13:25.920
all four steps are complete.

00:13:28.920 --> 00:13:31.640
In DCI programs, which you should go to

00:13:35.800 --> 00:13:38.520
for advice about success in your life,

00:13:41.560 --> 00:13:43.040
especially financial success--

00:13:44.480 --> 00:13:50.800
we will talk about four steps for good seeds and good goals.

00:13:54.040 --> 00:13:56.240
But here we're talking dzokpa--

00:13:56.680 --> 00:13:58.560
four steps for bad seeds.

00:14:01.080 --> 00:14:04.120
The minute you finish the fourth step,

00:14:04.160 --> 00:14:08.080
you're going to bed, you're doing anti-coffee meditation:

00:14:08.560 --> 00:14:11.720
"I'm so glad I ate the pork! Now I will have big muscles."

00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:25.000
The mind at that moment,

00:14:25.320 --> 00:14:28.000
the consciousness at that moment,

00:14:29.280 --> 00:14:31.520
where the seed is imprinted into.

00:14:31.720 --> 00:14:33.080
Here's the mind

00:14:35.200 --> 00:14:39.080
that's called the consciousness at the time of the cause.

00:14:43.160 --> 00:14:44.440
Because the seed is being planted,

00:14:44.640 --> 00:14:46.920
the cause is being planted

00:14:47.920 --> 00:14:49.920
into the consciousness.

00:14:50.520 --> 00:14:52.080
le dey tu la ten ne...
(LAS DE'I MTHU LA BRTEN NAS...)

00:14:52.080 --> 00:14:54.920
...nyelbay kye si du nying tsam jar ma takpay ne kap...
(...DMYAL BA'I SKYE SRID DU NYING MTSAMS SBYAR MA THAG PA'I GNAS SKABS)

00:14:54.920 --> 00:14:57.120
...kyi namshe dendre du kyi namshe yin
(...KYI RNAM SHES DE 'BRAS DUS KYI RNAM SHES YIN)--

00:14:57.360 --> 00:14:58.360
but,

00:14:58.360 --> 00:15:00.600
because of that power of that karma,

00:15:03.080 --> 00:15:06.520
you die and you cross the bridge

00:15:06.880 --> 00:15:10.120
into the new life to the hell realms.

00:15:17.160 --> 00:15:21.800
That mind travels from the life where you killed the pig

00:15:22.040 --> 00:15:24.920
up to the life you go to the hell.

00:15:33.760 --> 00:15:35.760
The moment you reach the hell,

00:15:37.840 --> 00:15:39.840
your mind at that time,

00:15:40.640 --> 00:15:44.400
we call it the consciousness of the time of the result.

00:15:48.320 --> 00:15:51.120
Then he makes another statement in the text.

00:15:51.120 --> 00:15:52.400
mi geway le...
(MI DGE BA'I LAS...)

00:15:55.040 --> 00:16:00.760
...re re kyang ngen song gi kyewa mangpo pen nu
(...RE RES KYANG NGAN SONG GI SKYE BA MANG PO 'PHEN NUS)--

00:16:02.920 --> 00:16:06.480
Each time you make bad karma,

00:16:08.680 --> 00:16:11.560
each time you eat an animal's body,

00:16:14.960 --> 00:16:18.160
each one of those eatings has the power

00:16:18.160 --> 00:16:21.320
to create many births in the lower realms.

00:16:30.640 --> 00:16:35.800
If that factory that kills the pig, they really make the pig suffer,

00:16:40.320 --> 00:16:42.400
and you eat pork,

00:16:43.560 --> 00:16:45.560
it's not one

00:16:45.960 --> 00:16:48.040
suffering life going to come from that many.

00:16:52.520 --> 00:16:54.080
That's the bad news.

00:16:54.560 --> 00:16:56.760
The next sentence has the goodness.

00:16:59.000 --> 00:17:02.040
de shin sunam kyi le sok la rik dre
(DE BZHIN BSOD NAMS KYI LAS SOGS LA RIGS 'GRE)--

00:17:02.040 --> 00:17:04.640
but when you make good karma,

00:17:08.080 --> 00:17:10.080
you can do the same thing.

00:17:11.120 --> 00:17:14.160
You make one nice tea for your friend,

00:17:16.320 --> 00:17:19.080
and you dedicate it to becoming a Buddha,

00:17:21.040 --> 00:17:25.760
that one making tea will give you many happy rebirths.

00:17:33.160 --> 00:17:36.600
How does that action of eating the pork,

00:17:36.640 --> 00:17:41.760
how does this imprint press on the mind? How does it happen?

00:17:46.400 --> 00:17:49.760
This is a big question in the Mind-Only School.

00:17:52.440 --> 00:17:57.640
We spent a long time discussing it in the Mixed Nuts translation classes.

00:18:03.160 --> 00:18:06.480
Those classes are free online on YouTube;

00:18:10.040 --> 00:18:12.040
Tibetan Language Channel,

00:18:14.040 --> 00:18:16.040
600 hours.

00:18:17.040 --> 00:18:18.840
You should look at them.

00:18:20.320 --> 00:18:22.400
detar che ma la num shukpa-am
(DE LTAR BYE MA LA SNUM ZHUGS PA'AM)--

00:18:23.120 --> 00:18:24.960
if you have sand

00:18:27.440 --> 00:18:30.000
and you drip oil on it ...

00:18:33.080 --> 00:18:36.840
In America, in the car fixing places,

00:18:39.840 --> 00:18:41.880
the oil will get on the floor,

00:18:43.080 --> 00:18:45.040
and it becomes very slippery,

00:18:46.320 --> 00:18:49.520
so they will spread sand on the floor.

00:18:54.040 --> 00:18:57.040
The sand will absorb the oil.

00:18:58.120 --> 00:19:03.400
And that's one example for how the consciousness absorbs the imprint.

00:19:08.680 --> 00:19:14.120
shok bu la tel tse gyabpa
(SHOG BU LA THEL TSE BRGYAB PA)--

00:19:15.280 --> 00:19:17.080
tel tse (THEL TSE) ...

00:19:19.640 --> 00:19:21.760
Right here, yeah, good, you don't know.

00:19:22.120 --> 00:19:26.040
I'll give you another Tibetan word: chakya (PHYAG RGYA).

00:19:28.640 --> 00:19:29.320
Yeah.

00:19:30.120 --> 00:19:32.120
What's the real meaning of mudra?

00:19:32.520 --> 00:19:35.720
This is twenty dollars. Okay, twenty dollars.

00:19:36.600 --> 00:19:39.200
tel tse is the other word for "stamp."

00:19:42.280 --> 00:19:47.400
In the old days, the great emperors would stamp the paper with their seal.

00:19:52.920 --> 00:19:57.120
That's another example for how the seed is imprinted on the mind.

00:20:01.320 --> 00:20:04.000
le kyi bakchak gupa
(LAS KYI BAG CHAGS BSGOS PA)

00:20:04.000 --> 00:20:05.400
gupa (BSGOS PA) here

00:20:06.440 --> 00:20:09.160
is an unusual Tibetan word.

00:20:12.640 --> 00:20:15.920
But it's an important word in the study of seeds.

00:20:18.680 --> 00:20:24.040
It almost means like, if you take a jasmine flower,

00:20:27.080 --> 00:20:29.440
and you wipe it on your clothes,

00:20:31.640 --> 00:20:34.840
then that smell will get into the cloth.

00:20:38.280 --> 00:20:41.080
What's another good word?

00:20:42.520 --> 00:20:44.520
It gets "imbued,"

00:20:47.200 --> 00:20:48.400
"infused."

00:20:50.120 --> 00:20:52.120
The smell gets infused.

00:20:53.880 --> 00:20:55.080
So you can say

00:20:55.960 --> 00:20:58.000
"imprinted."

00:20:59.600 --> 00:21:01.600
Or you can say "infused."

00:21:02.560 --> 00:21:04.240
shakpa la (BZHAG PA LA)--

00:21:04.960 --> 00:21:10.320
then that seed needs water and fertilizer,

00:21:13.520 --> 00:21:18.560
which is two kinds of desire: link number eight and link number nine.

00:21:23.440 --> 00:21:28.360
We'll talk about those two kinds of desire later, because they're not really desire.

00:21:32.680 --> 00:21:35.800
But link number eight and link number nine,

00:21:38.400 --> 00:21:40.720
they take the seed from link number two,

00:21:43.800 --> 00:21:46.920
which was infused into link number three: your mind.

00:21:50.120 --> 00:21:52.000
They water it, they give it fertilizer,

00:21:55.000 --> 00:21:58.000
and then that karma becomes extremely powerful.

00:22:00.040 --> 00:22:02.160
We'll talk about it later.

00:22:02.760 --> 00:22:04.520
We're going to go to link number four.

00:22:06.880 --> 00:22:10.160
This is called nama rupa: name and form.

00:22:12.880 --> 00:22:15.480
The image is two guys in a boat.

00:22:19.400 --> 00:22:21.320
If you remember

00:22:22.400 --> 00:22:25.040
in link number three, your mind was

00:22:25.040 --> 00:22:26.880
entering your mother's womb

00:22:32.000 --> 00:22:35.080
or into an egg, things like that.

00:22:40.320 --> 00:22:42.520
But talking about normal human birth,

00:22:45.080 --> 00:22:48.000
shipa ming suk la ngel kye kyi wang du je na
(BZHI PA MING GZUGS LA MNGAL SKYES KYI DBANG DU BYAS NA)--

00:22:48.440 --> 00:22:50.640
if we're going to talk about link number four--

00:22:53.000 --> 00:22:54.760
name and form--

00:22:55.760 --> 00:23:00.040
let's stick to people who are born from a womb.

00:23:04.120 --> 00:23:06.760
When you say "name,"

00:23:09.080 --> 00:23:15.560
it's really a reference to the four of the five parts of a person.

00:23:20.560 --> 00:23:22.560
So in English, we say "body and mind."

00:23:25.520 --> 00:23:28.160
But in Buddhism,

00:23:29.160 --> 00:23:30.760
we say "the five parts."

00:23:31.880 --> 00:23:34.320
Normally in English, we would just say "body and mind"--

00:23:36.160 --> 00:23:38.160
the physical part and the mental part.

00:23:41.120 --> 00:23:42.400
But in Buddhism,

00:23:43.840 --> 00:23:47.240
we divide body and mind into five parts.

00:23:49.840 --> 00:23:53.080
So four of them are called ming shiy pungpo (MING BZHI'I PHUNG PO),

00:23:53.200 --> 00:23:55.120
which means "the

00:23:55.320 --> 00:23:58.400
part of you which is called 'name'."

00:24:06.440 --> 00:24:12.120
It has ... four of the five parts are included into the "name" when you say "name and form."

00:24:18.040 --> 00:24:22.160
These are tsorwa dushe duche namshe (TSOR BA 'DU SHES 'DU BYED RNAM SHES)--these four.

00:24:23.280 --> 00:24:24.680
tsorwa (TSOR BA)--

00:24:25.280 --> 00:24:27.280
your feeling.

00:24:27.760 --> 00:24:29.880
Good feeling, bad feeling, neutral feeling.

00:24:31.840 --> 00:24:33.840
Body feeling, mental feeling.

00:24:35.920 --> 00:24:36.920
dushe ('DU SHES)--

00:24:37.440 --> 00:24:41.360
your habit of dividing things:

00:24:41.600 --> 00:24:47.040
that's big, that's small; that's tall, that's short; that's my friend, that's my enemy.

00:24:53.720 --> 00:24:59.160
duche ('DU BYED) means "other parts" of you, like the seeds in your mind.

00:25:07.760 --> 00:25:10.800
And namshe (RNAM SHES)--your mind.

00:25:11.640 --> 00:25:16.080
These four are called "name," when we say "name and form."

00:25:21.600 --> 00:25:26.120
Basically, you can think of these four as your mind inside your mother's womb.

00:25:34.040 --> 00:25:39.680
namshe shukpay ku trak gi mer merpo sok ni suk kyi tendrel te
(RNAM SHES ZHUGS PA'I KHU KHRAG GI MER MER PO SOGS NI GZUGS KYI RTEN 'BREL TE)

00:25:39.840 --> 00:25:43.160
What is the "form" part of "name and form"?

00:25:47.520 --> 00:25:52.400
In the very first moments inside your mom's womb,

00:25:56.520 --> 00:26:02.280
it's the mother's menstrual blood and the father's semen, which are mixing together,

00:26:05.880 --> 00:26:09.000
and your mind goes into it at link number three.

00:26:12.160 --> 00:26:19.360
That's pretty much your body at that moment--it's just a little puddle of blood and semen.

00:26:23.440 --> 00:26:27.200
Here there's a very unusual word: mer merpo (MER MER PO).

00:26:30.760 --> 00:26:38.040
This refers to the first of ten stages of life of a human.

00:26:42.160 --> 00:26:46.200
These are .... how do you say ...hmmm

00:26:51.840 --> 00:26:53.840
I'm going to teach you those ten,

00:26:55.000 --> 00:26:56.360
because I like to go deeper

00:26:58.120 --> 00:27:00.320
and he mentions the first,

00:27:01.080 --> 00:27:03.000
which is called mer merpo.

00:27:04.120 --> 00:27:08.000
It kind of means little sticky mess,

00:27:10.920 --> 00:27:12.480
blood and semen together,

00:27:13.320 --> 00:27:15.800
and that's your body at that moment.

00:27:18.160 --> 00:27:24.160
Pabongka Rinpoche says--before I go on to those ten,

00:27:26.160 --> 00:27:27.640
which is extra,

00:27:28.040 --> 00:27:29.520
it's just to go deeper--

00:27:32.000 --> 00:27:37.120
he says maybe we should call this link number four,

00:27:41.920 --> 00:27:44.760
instead of calling it "name and form,"

00:27:47.040 --> 00:27:49.280
which is really "mind and body."

00:27:51.320 --> 00:27:55.440
Maybe we should call it either mind or body, at that moment.

00:28:00.680 --> 00:28:05.240
Which part are you focusing on is the link at that moment.

00:28:10.920 --> 00:28:14.520
I did some work and I got what I think is the best explanation

00:28:15.000 --> 00:28:18.200
of the ten stages of life that starts with mer merpo,

00:28:19.880 --> 00:28:22.080
which is that little mess of liquids.

00:28:34.160 --> 00:28:40.120
This comes from a very famous commentary on vowed morality-- vinaya.

00:28:52.680 --> 00:28:57.800
It's written by Tsonawa Sherab Sangpo (MTSO SNA BA SHES RAB BZANG PO).

00:28:58.760 --> 00:29:01.480
He lived about two hundred years before Tsongkapa.

00:29:05.400 --> 00:29:09.800
He wrote a brilliant two-volume commentary on vowed morality.

00:29:17.760 --> 00:29:20.040
It's called a chen dril (CHEN DRIL).

00:29:20.880 --> 00:29:25.520
chen dril means a commentary where there are also some footnotes.

00:29:29.120 --> 00:29:34.080
Actually, I took the footnotes out of this section because it's too complicated.

00:29:38.080 --> 00:29:40.800
But still, it's a beautiful description.

00:29:43.440 --> 00:29:45.880
We're going to go through this part,

00:29:47.920 --> 00:29:50.000
it's going to take some extra time.

00:29:51.560 --> 00:29:53.560
I hope you'll be patient with me

00:29:55.400 --> 00:29:57.400
and don't complain you're getting extra.

00:29:59.400 --> 00:30:01.640
Ok, here we go. We're going to follow the Tibetan.

00:30:03.720 --> 00:30:06.400
mir gyurpa la ne skab chur ye te
(MIR GYUR PA LA GNAS SKABS BCUR DBYE STE)--

00:30:07.800 --> 00:30:09.600
Let's say you happen to be a human,

00:30:11.840 --> 00:30:15.560
your life can be divided into ten stages of life.

00:30:18.680 --> 00:30:23.760
Shakespeare wrote a beautiful little text about the stages of life.

00:30:29.040 --> 00:30:32.160
I'm going to give you that at the end--that's dessert.

00:30:37.280 --> 00:30:43.680
u den le ('OD LDAN LAS) means the commentary to vowed morality which shines like light.

00:30:54.040 --> 00:30:57.200
That was written maybe more than a thousand years ago.

00:31:01.800 --> 00:31:06.240
Now he is quoting this older Vinaya book from India.

00:31:10.520 --> 00:31:11.800
mir chakpa ni (MIR CHAGS PA NI)--

00:31:12.160 --> 00:31:15.240
The stages of human life

00:31:19.120 --> 00:31:21.120
number one: mer mer (MER MER),

00:31:21.440 --> 00:31:22.600
nur nur (NUR NUR)--number two,

00:31:23.920 --> 00:31:25.360
number three: tar tar (LTAR LTAR),

00:31:26.680 --> 00:31:28.680
number four: trang gyur ('KHRANG 'GYUR),

00:31:29.840 --> 00:31:32.000
number five: kang lak gyu (RKANG LAG 'GYUS),

00:31:33.520 --> 00:31:35.080
number six: yipa (BYIS PA),

00:31:36.200 --> 00:31:39.120
number seven: shon nu (GZHON NU)

00:31:40.040 --> 00:31:42.040
number eight: ngel bap (DNGAL BABS),

00:31:43.040 --> 00:31:45.040
number nine: barma (BAR MA),

00:31:45.520 --> 00:31:47.280
number ten: genpo (RGAN PO).

00:31:48.080 --> 00:31:50.080
These are the ten.

00:31:51.720 --> 00:31:53.720
He explains what the ten are.

00:31:55.400 --> 00:31:59.040
The ancient commentary was written by Shakyaprabha.

00:32:03.160 --> 00:32:05.400
He doesn't really explain the ten much.

00:32:07.680 --> 00:32:09.960
So here's Tsonawa's comment.

00:32:12.080 --> 00:32:14.080
de nam kyi kyepar ni
(DE RNAMS KYI KHYAD PAR NI)

00:32:14.440 --> 00:32:16.600
What's the difference between these ten?

00:32:19.160 --> 00:32:21.120
pa may mi tsangwa nyi tsok shing
(PHA MA'I MI GTZANG BA GNYIS TSOGS SHING)--

00:32:21.400 --> 00:32:26.040
when the two, he calls it dirty liquids,

00:32:30.960 --> 00:32:33.000
from your mom and your dad,

00:32:34.160 --> 00:32:38.040
when they mix together in the womb,

00:32:41.160 --> 00:32:45.680
the mind from the bardo (BAR DO) enters that blood and semen.

00:32:51.560 --> 00:32:56.120
During the first week of the formation of the fetus,

00:33:01.000 --> 00:33:03.320
we call it mer merpo.

00:33:05.480 --> 00:33:07.480
What's it mean?

00:33:08.560 --> 00:33:11.680
And here it's misspelled--pri ma tabu (misspelled: SBRIS MA LTA BUS).

00:33:15.720 --> 00:33:17.720
You know a pond of water?

00:33:20.080 --> 00:33:21.040
Or Indian tea

00:33:22.600 --> 00:33:25.040
and you pour in the milk.

00:33:26.320 --> 00:33:30.400
You boil it, and then when it gets cool,

00:33:32.080 --> 00:33:36.920
we call it scum--there's a layer on the top that gets a little bit hard.

00:33:40.640 --> 00:33:42.640
That's a pri ma (SPRIS MA)

00:33:42.920 --> 00:33:47.040
or a very dirty pond that has a layer of scum.

00:33:47.600 --> 00:33:51.040
Scum means like super dirty stuff on the top.

00:33:55.200 --> 00:34:02.000
That's what you look like in the first week--you're like some scum of the cream or something.

00:34:08.160 --> 00:34:11.720
They gave that a name called mer merpo,

00:34:11.800 --> 00:34:15.200
which doesn't mean a lot in Tibetan. It just means icky gooey stuff.

00:34:20.040 --> 00:34:21.680
dun trak nyipa la
(BDUN PHRAG GNYIS PA LA)--

00:34:22.000 --> 00:34:24.520
in the second week of development in the womb,

00:34:28.200 --> 00:34:31.320
you take a shape we call nur nurpo (NUR NUR PO).

00:34:34.800 --> 00:34:36.440
sho tabur duk
(ZHO LTA BUR 'DUG)--

00:34:36.920 --> 00:34:40.040
your body is a little bit like yogurt.

00:34:43.040 --> 00:34:44.560
shar ma gyur pa-o
(SHAR MA GYUR PA'O)--

00:34:45.120 --> 00:34:47.000
and it starts to form into

00:34:47.840 --> 00:34:50.000
like a flat piece of cloth,

00:34:50.600 --> 00:34:52.600
like a strip,

00:34:56.080 --> 00:34:58.240
like a ribbon.

00:35:03.200 --> 00:35:04.880
That's called nur nur.

00:35:05.080 --> 00:35:09.480
You're a little bit longer, but you are skinny like tape.

00:35:16.200 --> 00:35:18.960
dun trak sumpa la
('DUN PHRAG GSUM PA LA)--in the third week,

00:35:19.800 --> 00:35:22.280
tar telpo (LTAR LTAL PO)--you get tar telpo

00:35:23.040 --> 00:35:26.680
and that little strip ribbon, of flesh,

00:35:26.920 --> 00:35:29.120
becomes a little bit wider--

00:35:29.120 --> 00:35:32.120
you can see it almost starting to become a cylinder.

00:35:40.120 --> 00:35:42.040
dun trak shipa ne
(BDUN PHRAG BZHI PA NAS)--

00:35:42.040 --> 00:35:43.160
in the fourth week,

00:35:44.080 --> 00:35:45.680
we call tre gyur ('KHRAD 'GYUR)--

00:35:45.960 --> 00:35:49.080
as you start to get more stiff

00:35:52.480 --> 00:35:54.720
kabar gyur te men du
(BSKA BAR GYUR TE MNAN DU).

00:35:55.960 --> 00:35:59.880
In English, you take some body like a cylinder,

00:36:01.520 --> 00:36:06.480
and you can actually push on it and it will stay like that,

00:36:10.680 --> 00:36:14.440
a little bit firm.

00:36:15.360 --> 00:36:17.360
Ok, step number five:

00:36:18.160 --> 00:36:22.000
kang lak gyupa ni sha hlak tabur gyur te
(RKANG LAG 'GYUS PA NI SHA LHAG LTA BUR GYUR TE)--

00:36:22.000 --> 00:36:26.080
they don't say the week, but the next step is called

00:36:27.200 --> 00:36:29.720
arms and legs are starting to squeeze out.

00:36:35.360 --> 00:36:37.400
Like if you get a

00:36:38.920 --> 00:36:43.440
goiter on the throat, you get a big bump come here.

00:36:44.360 --> 00:36:46.360
Or you get a wart on your face.

00:36:48.680 --> 00:36:52.200
So then the kid's arms and legs are in like bumps.

00:36:58.240 --> 00:37:00.000
Stage number six

00:37:01.400 --> 00:37:03.680
called yipa (BYIS PA). You know this word--

00:37:04.240 --> 00:37:06.120
you had it for a non-arya.

00:37:07.280 --> 00:37:09.280
It means ...

00:37:09.640 --> 00:37:11.760
It means an infant.

00:37:12.560 --> 00:37:13.840
In English, infant.

00:37:14.200 --> 00:37:15.680
And the definition

00:37:17.040 --> 00:37:19.040
is that you came out of your mom

00:37:20.760 --> 00:37:24.040
but you can't walk or crawl--you are just stuck there.

00:37:29.400 --> 00:37:32.200
And Stanley knows this word because it's also used in Buddhist philosophy

00:37:33.040 --> 00:37:36.920
to describe a person who hasn't seen emptiness yet.

00:37:46.120 --> 00:37:49.680
They're like a little baby who can't even crawl.

00:37:54.320 --> 00:37:56.320
Stage number seven:

00:37:58.040 --> 00:38:02.880
shon nu ni dro nu ne dupa chu mi nupa-o
(GZHON NU NI 'GRO NUS NAS 'DOD PA SPYOD MI NUS PA'O)--

00:38:03.160 --> 00:38:05.840
from the time that you can crawl

00:38:08.200 --> 00:38:12.800
up to the time that your body is mature enough to have a sexual experience.

00:38:19.560 --> 00:38:21.560
That's called youth.

00:38:27.880 --> 00:38:29.640
The next one is called

00:38:30.240 --> 00:38:31.600
dar la babpa
(DAR LA BAB PA)--

00:38:32.080 --> 00:38:34.520
I mispronounced it before--I said ngel bap,

00:38:34.720 --> 00:38:39.080
but the carving was wrong. It's dar la babpa.

00:38:40.560 --> 00:38:46.720
dar la babpa ni dupa chu nu...
(DAR LA BAB PA NI 'DOD PA SPYOD NUS...)

00:38:47.640 --> 00:38:50.520
...pa ne lo sum chu men che do
(...PA NAS LO SUM CU MAN CHAD DO)--

00:38:50.800 --> 00:38:55.040
from the time that you are old enough to have your first sexual experience

00:38:55.400 --> 00:38:59.520
up to the time of thirty is called young adult.

00:39:01.360 --> 00:39:03.360
Up to the age of thirty, yup.

00:39:20.000 --> 00:39:21.920
bar ma ni
(BAR MA NI)--

00:39:22.160 --> 00:39:24.160
then what we call...

00:39:25.160 --> 00:39:27.880
What did we say? Young adult, right? Middle age.

00:39:28.800 --> 00:39:33.160
In English, we call it middle age and in Tibetan same,

00:39:33.840 --> 00:39:36.360
but it means from thirty

00:39:38.280 --> 00:39:40.120
on up to fifty.

00:39:41.360 --> 00:39:43.600
Stage number nine:

00:39:44.760 --> 00:39:46.760
middle age.

00:39:49.000 --> 00:39:52.080
Stage number ten is called elderly.

00:39:55.040 --> 00:39:57.200
Starts at age fifty,

00:39:59.320 --> 00:40:01.880
but for some people at sixty-eight, okay?

00:40:03.600 --> 00:40:05.600
Just kidding.

00:40:08.000 --> 00:40:10.000
Why are we talking about the stages?

00:40:11.520 --> 00:40:13.520
Because we heard the first stage

00:40:15.440 --> 00:40:18.600
and it was inside the womb.

00:40:20.960 --> 00:40:28.880
It was just the five parts of you stuck to the blood and semen of your dad and mom,

00:40:29.120 --> 00:40:31.320
like your new body.

00:40:41.080 --> 00:40:43.120
Name and form:

00:40:43.760 --> 00:40:45.800
all your mental parts, etc.,

00:40:48.040 --> 00:40:50.040
along with your physical part,

00:40:51.160 --> 00:40:53.200
in the womb at the first moment.

00:40:55.640 --> 00:41:00.160
The body and mind inside the womb,

00:41:03.000 --> 00:41:04.600
that's link number four.

00:41:05.760 --> 00:41:08.080
Two guys in a boat because the boat represents the womb.

00:41:13.280 --> 00:41:19.920
You can see it in the picture here, even if it was drawn by a bunch of kids.

00:41:22.600 --> 00:41:24.640
There's a body and mind, two guys in a boat,

00:41:25.120 --> 00:41:26.600
which is the womb of the mom.

00:41:31.720 --> 00:41:35.480
Whenever I teach this--and this is the last thing for today's session--

00:41:39.200 --> 00:41:41.720
I love to go through a quotation by Shakespeare.

00:41:45.000 --> 00:41:50.080
It's very, very famous from a play called "As You Like It," which is kind of a comedy.

00:41:58.240 --> 00:42:00.240
So just sit back and relax.

00:42:06.800 --> 00:42:12.080
Put it in the Tibetan stuff to show on the screen so Tim can follow in the English if you want.

00:42:16.840 --> 00:42:20.720
All the world is a stage, like a play,

00:42:21.920 --> 00:42:25.480
and all the men and women are just actors on the stage.

00:42:28.800 --> 00:42:30.640
Each has their exit and their entrance--

00:42:30.640 --> 00:42:35.520
there's time when they're supposed to leave this stage and there's a time when they're supposed to come on the stage--

00:42:35.520 --> 00:42:36.920
like death and rebirth.

00:42:44.520 --> 00:42:48.480
And in our lifetime, we play seven different actors.

00:42:53.440 --> 00:42:56.120
First we are the infant--yipa.

00:42:59.080 --> 00:43:03.640
Mewling and puking in his nurse's arm, nurse is the woman they hire to hold the baby.

00:43:05.840 --> 00:43:08.680
Mewling means "weh weh" and puking is "ble ble."

00:43:18.520 --> 00:43:21.400
Then the second part we all play--

00:43:24.240 --> 00:43:27.120
it's like the same as the ten parts of the Vinaya--

00:43:30.200 --> 00:43:32.960
then you are the whining schoolboy,

00:43:34.480 --> 00:43:36.480
"Oh ma, do I have to go to school?"

00:43:37.920 --> 00:43:43.280
"Yeah, take your satchel," means your backpack with all your books and

00:43:45.680 --> 00:43:47.280
your shining morning face.

00:43:47.280 --> 00:43:53.320
It means your life is like one day and in the morning the face is very fresh and beautiful.

00:44:03.960 --> 00:44:07.080
He agrees to go to school but he goes as fast as a snail.

00:44:12.480 --> 00:44:15.280
Then he gets, I don't know, sixteen years old,

00:44:17.040 --> 00:44:19.040
then he falls in love,

00:44:20.280 --> 00:44:22.280
he or she falls in love--

00:44:23.400 --> 00:44:25.400
first time in high school.

00:44:26.240 --> 00:44:28.080
Then they sigh like a furnace.

00:44:28.280 --> 00:44:32.640
Furnace means an old thing to make the fire go...

00:44:33.000 --> 00:44:35.000
it's like (blowing sounds).

00:44:39.280 --> 00:44:41.920
"Oh, oh, my boyfriend!" "Oh, my girlfriend!"

00:44:44.200 --> 00:44:48.880
With a woeful ballad, means like a rock'n'roll song, which is like "Oh, she don't love me."

00:44:54.640 --> 00:45:00.920
He sent to his mistress's eyebrow, he gets up close to his girlfriend and says, "I love you, I love you."

00:45:07.480 --> 00:45:09.480
Then later they get more mature,

00:45:11.200 --> 00:45:13.200
they want to fight in the war

00:45:15.160 --> 00:45:18.880
full of strange oaths, "I will defend my country no matter what."

00:45:24.720 --> 00:45:28.040
Now they can grow a beard--"pard like" means "like a priest."

00:45:33.400 --> 00:45:36.080
Jealous in honor, sudden and quick in quarrel.

00:45:36.120 --> 00:45:38.080
You say something to these guys. They're like, "I will fight you!"

00:45:41.720 --> 00:45:43.880
Very brave real (Chinese word).

00:45:47.680 --> 00:45:51.000
Seeking the bubble of reputation, they want to be famous.

00:45:55.120 --> 00:45:59.600
But that kind of famous tough guy lasts like as long as a bubble.

00:46:05.920 --> 00:46:09.080
Even in the mouth of the cannon, even when they're about to die,

00:46:15.880 --> 00:46:17.880
then they come back from the war,

00:46:19.440 --> 00:46:20.560
they eat

00:46:21.880 --> 00:46:23.440
too much

00:46:24.080 --> 00:46:26.080
pastries,

00:46:27.760 --> 00:46:29.760
they start to gain a little bit of weight,

00:46:31.920 --> 00:46:33.920
they start to collect money,

00:46:35.920 --> 00:46:38.640
then they have better clothes,

00:46:40.120 --> 00:46:43.680
and they are very intelligent and they look at you like this (frowns).

00:46:46.280 --> 00:46:50.120
Then they start quoting wise things.

00:46:52.560 --> 00:46:54.280
They give you logic.

00:46:55.200 --> 00:46:57.040
They are more mature,

00:46:57.680 --> 00:47:00.040
like they became a lawyer.

00:47:00.440 --> 00:47:04.000
and he also plays--he's the fifth part of a human.

00:47:07.400 --> 00:47:09.400
What is stage number six?

00:47:10.880 --> 00:47:16.720
The guy's legs gets... those big muscle legs from his war time, they get skinny, skinny.

00:47:20.880 --> 00:47:24.040
Then the pants, they're not tight anymore,

00:47:27.440 --> 00:47:30.400
then he has to wear glasses also,

00:47:32.320 --> 00:47:35.160
and he gets to a little special belly for a sixty-seven year old.

00:47:39.600 --> 00:47:42.400
His socks don't fit him anymore because they're too skinny.

00:47:46.800 --> 00:47:48.800
He used to talk like that (deep voice),

00:47:52.160 --> 00:47:54.160
like a little kid (high voice).

00:48:02.200 --> 00:48:05.440
He loses ... even the voice becomes weak.

00:48:08.000 --> 00:48:11.120
Then comes the last scene of all--number seven.

00:48:15.160 --> 00:48:17.480
It ends this strange story.

00:48:21.880 --> 00:48:24.280
He goes back to his childhood,

00:48:28.040 --> 00:48:30.040
can't think anymore,

00:48:32.040 --> 00:48:34.040
you lose your teeth,

00:48:34.040 --> 00:48:35.120
lose the eyes,

00:48:35.120 --> 00:48:38.080
lose all the taste of the good food,

00:48:39.840 --> 00:48:41.960
lose everything.

00:48:43.720 --> 00:48:46.200
And that's Shakespeare's seven stages.

00:48:50.400 --> 00:48:52.400
It's not much different from the Wheel of Life,

00:48:55.000 --> 00:48:58.920
same result get old and die.

00:49:00.200 --> 00:49:04.920
That's all caused, because we don't understand our husband in the kitchen.

00:49:09.120 --> 00:49:11.120
And we don't have to go like that.

00:49:13.200 --> 00:49:14.560
We can change it,

00:49:15.520 --> 00:49:20.360
if we change the misunderstanding of our husband in the kitchen.

00:49:23.560 --> 00:49:25.560
Okay, we'll continue with the Wheel of Life

00:49:28.000 --> 00:49:29.320
session 14

00:49:30.760 --> 00:49:32.040
in the next class.

00:49:32.560 --> 00:49:34.760
Thank you. And thank you Stanley for translating.

